# Cursor Rules — Autonomous Income Node

## Project Overview
Autonomous AI agent (Node.js 20 + TypeScript) that generates USDC income on Base blockchain.
Uses a ReAct loop with Claude Sonnet, multi-model routing (Haiku triage), technical indicators,
and autonomous research. Runs 24/7 in Docker with Cloudflare Tunnel.

## Critical Files
- `CLAUDE.md` — full project context, read this first
- `src/agent/index.ts` — AgentCore startup sequence
- `src/agent/react-loop.ts` — main ReAct loop
- `src/agent/model-router.ts` — Haiku triage before Sonnet
- `src/strategies/trading/feature-engine.ts` — technical indicators (EMA, RSI, MACD, ATR, BB)
- `src/strategies/trading/kill-switch.ts` — emergency stop ($5/day, $15 total)
- `src/survival/index.ts` — tier management
- `.env` — production secrets (never show in output)

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode, ESM, NodeNext module resolution
- All imports need `.js` extension (ESM requirement)
- Use `bigint` for USDC amounts (6 decimal precision: $1 = 1_000000n)
- Never log secrets — use `maskSecrets()` from `src/config/log-filter.ts`
- Error handling: never throw in production modules, return null/Result pattern

## Architecture Rules
- All external integrations go through MCP servers in `src/mcp/servers/`
- Agent wallet at `keys/keystore.json` — AES-256 encrypted with WALLET_PASSWORD
- Blockchain: Base mainnet (chainId 8453), USDC `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913`
- Never modify `constitution.md` — protected by hash verification
- Tier gates: check `getCapabilityGates(tier)` before any strategy
- Pre-cycle hooks: AutoLender → MultiSourceScanner → FeatureEngine (before each LLM call)
- ModelRouter: Haiku triage decides if Sonnet is needed (saves ~70% LLM costs)

